#coding:utf-8

"""
ID:          n/a
ISSUE:       n/a
TITLE:       External tables must accept values of all existing FB datatypes if they belong to allowed range (or set), and must reject out-of-range values
DESCRIPTION:
    [text generated by zcode.ai]
    Single test function loops over ALL existing FB datatypes (see TYPES_DATA).
    For every datatype a dedicated external table is created, then several
    valid values are inserted (must succeed), then several invalid values are
    inserted (each must fail), and finally stored data is selected back and
    compared with expected output. Table is dropped when its part of the
    check completes. Overall outcome (PASSED / FAILED) relates to ALL of
    these checks; if at least one check fails, its datatype and concrete
    literals that were used in INSERT statements are shown in the assert message.

    No ISQL is launched by this test at all: single connection to the test DB
    is made via python firebird-driver (see drv_connect(...) call), and all
    statements are executed using its cursor. Expected data for every datatype
    are two blocks: EXPECTED_STDOUT (rows that SELECT must return, one line per
    row, values converted to str) and EXPECTED_STDERR (text of DatabaseError
    that each of invalid INSERT must raise, one block per statement).
    Actual data are collected into single list (rows first, then errors) and
    compared with union of these two expected blocks.
NOTES:
    [11.09.2026] zcode.ai
    1. Test is developed on the base of re-implemented test_external_file_03_d.py.
       It uses ConfigManager class from QA-plugin in order to preserve original
       content of databases.conf and restore it at the teardown stage.
       Copy of $FB_HOME/databases.conf will be stored in the folder where test database lives.
       New content of this file will define alias that points to test DB file
       (see 'CONNECT_TO_ALIAS') and parameter for enabling creation of
       external table which storage is in the same folder as test DB uses:
           ExternalFileAccess = Restrict {test_db_path}
    2. Connection charset = utf8: this is required for inserting Georgian text
       into varchar(64) character set utf8 and for check that such text can NOT
       be inserted into varchar(64) iso8859_1 ("Cannot transliterate character
       between character sets").
    3. One need to be sure that firebird.conf does NOT contain DatabaseAccess = None.
    4. The firebird.conf must contain 'ExternalFileAccess = None'.

    ###############
    ### FACTS (probed on 6.0.0.2176) ###
    ###############
    1. External tables do NOT enforce declared PRECISION of decimal/numeric columns:
       only the range of their UNDERLYING storage (scaled int16/int32/int64/int128)
       is checked. E.g., insert of literal 1.00 into decimal(2,2) silently stores 1.00,
       and 327.68 into decimal(2,2) is stored too (see item 2). Because of this,
       'invalid' values for decimal/numeric in TYPES_DATA target overflow of the
       backing storage rather than declared precision.
    2. Backing storage differs for decimal and numeric when p = 1..4:
       decimal -> int32 (327.68 into decimal(2,2) is STORED), numeric -> int16
       (327.68 into numeric(2,2) fails with SQLSTATE = 22003 / 'numeric value is
       out of range', but -327.68 is stored because scaled -32768 FITS smallint).
    3. FB accepts date literals in 'DD.MM.YYYY' format but NOT 'DD-MM-YYYY':
       insert of '29-02-2004' fails with SQLSTATE = 22018 / conversion error.
    4. binary(64)/varbinary(64)/char(64) octets/varbinary: value that exceeds column
       length fails with SQLSTATE = 22001 / '-string right truncation -expected
       length 64, actual 65'.
    5. Time zone region validation: '01:02:03 Qwerty/Asdfgh' fails with
       SQLSTATE = 22009 / 'Invalid time zone region: Qwerty/Asdfgh'.
    6. Error texts in EXPECTED_STDERR are str(DatabaseError), i.e. they do NOT
       contain 'Statement failed, SQLSTATE = ...' header that ISQL adds.
    7. Rows in EXPECTED_STDOUT are captured with str() of every column value.
       repr() was rejected because for time/timestamp WITH TIME ZONE it contains
       tzinfo repr ('tzfile(...)' / 'tzwin(...)') which depends on implementation
       of tz database in Python, not on Firebird output.

    [12.09.2026] pzotov
    1. Source code, description and comments have been generated by zcode.ai.
       Current view was obtained after two suggestions.
       Several boundary values were added to double precision and decfloat datatypes.
       Added literal 'vérité' to almost all checks (must raise conversion error).
    2. This test superceedes following obsolete tests in $QA_HOME/tests/functional/gtcs/
       folder:
           test_external_file_03_d.py
           test_external_file_04_d.py
           test_external_file_04_d_bigint.py
           test_external_file_04_d_int128.py
           test_external_file_06_d.py
           test_external_file_09_d.py 
       All of them can be SKIPPED from execution.

    Checked on 6.0.0.2176; 5.0.5.1862; 4.0.8.3314.
"""

